;Match details

* '''Match 1: Maeda def. Stan (forfeit).''' The Speed Star's hollow points. Stan, recovering from surgery in Vaiahi, forfeited his final scheduled match; Maeda received the win without a bell. Maeda finishes 5-4, 10 points, the block's best outside run ending with a forfeit gift. '''Crowd:''' Applause for Stan's war, warm and brief.

* '''Match 2: Vance def. Morita.''' The perfect block, completed. Morita — 1-7, winless in the ring, the man the whole tour has adopted — gave the Workhorse his hardest fight of the night that wasn't the main event. The crowd sang for eleven minutes. The Drill Driver at 11:19 ended it. Vance is 8-0-1, 17 points, the block won with a round's worth of drama never required. '''Crowd:''' '''MORITA''' chants, louder than the '''VANCE''' chants. '''SPEAK''' chants on the walk-out. He did not. Toyozawa applauded the silence anyway — and the Workhorse stood at the top of the ramp and watched the main event.

* '''Match 3: Kengo def. Honda.''' The Cannon Club's last leader against the block's most honest man, their first meeting of the tournament. Honda's grappling made Kengo work; the shortcut was the Cannon Cutter out of nowhere at 13:02. Kengo finishes 5-4, 10 points, half of them hollow. Honda finishes 2-6-1, 5 points — every one of them wrestled. '''Crowd:''' BOOS for Kengo, respect applause for Honda. The AOPW man bowed to the crowd and walked out clean.

* '''Match 4: Marauder def. Nakamura.''' The mystery man against the artist, the block's last question answered cold. Nakamura's theater met the no-sell, and the chokeslam at 14:44 ended it. The Marauder finishes 5-4, 10 points — legitimate in the ring, cold outside it, and gone. Nakamura finishes 2-7, 4 points. '''Crowd:''' BOOS for the Marauder, applause for Nakamura's bow. The mystery man walked out through the crowd, unidentified, unhurried, one last time.

* '''Match 5: Leoni vs. Kawada — DRAW (30:00).''' The main event, the block's decider, and the draw that decided it. Kawada needed the win to clear the champion outright; Leoni needed it to hold the tiebreaker. Both men fought like the block was on the line, because it was. The Spear connected at 24 — Kawada kicked out at 2.9. The top-rope brainbuster at 27 — the champion kicked out at 2.8. The final minute was the two men on their knees, trading forearms, the crowd on its feet, and the bell at 30:00 found them standing. No winner. The block went to Vance. '''Crowd:''' '''LEONI''' and '''KAWADA''' chants in alternation for the full thirty. STANDING OVATION at the bell — the second of the tournament. Both men stood in the ring until the other left.

