''Note: [[Big Stan]] withdrew from the tournament on September 16. His remaining matches (Rounds 6–9) were recorded as forfeit losses, with each opponent receiving two points. Maeda's Round 9 win is a forfeit result.''

== Storyline notes ==

* '''Vance wins Block A.''' 8-0-1, 17 points, the only blemish the 30:00 draw with the champion on Day 9. The Workhorse never spoke, never needed to, and never lost. He goes to the Aizawa Dome on October 18 to face the Block B winner — and then, the champion at Wrestling Summit.
* '''The draw that decided it.''' Leoni 15, Kawada 15 — the champion unbeaten with three draws, the ace with one loss and one draw, and neither man able to finish the other in thirty minutes. The block's soul was decided by mathematics, and the mathematics said the Workhorse.
* '''Morita's G1 ends.''' 1-8, 2 points, winless in the ring — and the crowd sang for him for eleven minutes against the block winner. The tour's conscience closes with the loudest loss of the tournament.
* '''Kengo's hollow 10.''' 5-4, 10 points, half of them forfeit gifts or shortcuts. The Cannon Club's last leader finished the G1 the way he wrestled it: alive on paper, empty in the ring.
* '''The Marauder departs.''' 5-4, 10 points, the no-sell legitimate, the mystery intact. He kicked out of the Spear of Fangatapu and lost every match that mattered after. The block will not see him again — unless it does.

